{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And it shall come to pass.</b> [He will remove] his yoke — that of the king of Assyria." "And the kaph of <b>your neck</b> [refers] to Judah." "<b>And the strap.</b> Like destruction, and so too וחבל את מעשה ידיך (Ecclesiastes 5:5). Its meaning: and the yoke shall be destroyed, as when oil is placed on the neck. And the sense is that Judah shall grow strong."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:18.001193089Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}